  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Burma Investment Climate and Private Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment comprises a number of activities, however the largest value activity is the Investment Climate and Competativeness Program (ICCP). The other activity is for the provision of policy advice to the Myanmar Government.

 The Investment Climate and Competitiveness Program (ICCP) is a five-year program, co-funded with the UK Government&apos;s Department for International Development (DFID) that aims to improve the competitiveness of the private sector, increase investment and create jobs. The ICCP is implemented by the International Finance Corporation (IFC), part of the World Bank Group, under the Private Sector Development window of the World Bank Multi Donor Trust Fund (MDTF). Australia has committed up to $20 million from 2015-20, DFID has committed up to 10 million pounds (about $17 million).</narrative>
  </description>
